<title>UK: IGC revises 1997-98 world coarse grain trade up.</title>
<headline>IGC revises 1997-98 world coarse grain trade up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Grains Council on Thursday raised its estimate for 1997-98 world coarse grains trade to 91.7 million tonnes from its previous estimate of 91.4 million.</p>
<p>In its latest Grain Market Report it put 1996-97 imports at 88.8 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The estimated rise in 1997-98 imports is the result of rises of 100,000 tonnes each for Venezuela, Iran and South Africa.</p>
<p>All of the increase is in maize imports, the IGC said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
